From 0cafbc3440e28523ab142abda228b7b8df110cf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:35:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wip: apu-expert-gtt P1.1 + P2 + P3a/P3b/P3c -- a mlocked GTT
 expert store, the tier as a serving ARENA, the MTP head pinned outside the
 budget, one store shared safely by two models, the fills on r262's adaptive
 read transport, the buffered arm reading straight into the arena slot, and
 the RDNA3_5 UMA start arm
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A UMA-only resident expert tier: ONE anonymous region (mmap + MADV_HUGEPAGE), registered ONCE
with cudaHostRegister(Mapped|ReadOnly) and mlocked, that the hottest MoE expert tables are placed
in (P2) or that serves as the expert cache's ARENA (P3) and that MUL_MAT_ID reads in place -- with
no host pool and no slab arena below it.

- the region + first-fit allocator + census live in ggml/src/ggml-cuda/gtt-expert-store.{cu,cuh};
  the buffer type is in ggml-cuda.cu on the KV-region pattern (a DEVICE buft with the plain device
  type's vtable contract and a per-device unique name), and device hooks let the model loader open
  it, ask what it may lock, and print its census.
- -lme sizes it (P1.1): N GiB exactly, or auto = MOE_HOST_LIMIT_FRAC of MemAvailable, capped at
  the set and at RLIMIT_MEMLOCK; the SAME budget and the SAME heat ranking as the discrete arm,
  decided before any tensor is placed.  It engages without -ncmoe, and common/arg.cpp gains the
  UMA branch of the help text.
- P2 (a set that FITS the store): whole expert tables are placed in it and read in place.  The
  fill is the buffered pread arm, straight from the GGUF into the slot.
- P3 (a set that does NOT fit, MOE_EXPERT_GTT_ARENA=1, opt-in): the store becomes the cache's
  arena -- try_arena() is its third slot source beside the slab and cudaMalloc -- the expert
  tensors become HOLES in the read-only model mapping (nothing allocated, nothing pinned), and the
  delivery's existing LFRU residency serves every read.  g_cold_uva is false for the tier by
  construction (an APU's cold source would be a pageable page the GPU cannot address), so every
  miss evicts and fills.  The tier forces a MAPPED load: an iGPU reports no mmap_support, and a
  copied master would be a pageable full copy of the expert set.
- mlock is what makes it a RESERVATION: probe 16 (MEASUREMENTS.md §15) measured that a
  registered-only region is RECLAIMABLE under pressure -- the kernel splits its huge pages, swaps
  0-436 MiB per 2 GiB out, the next GPU read stalls a one-off 12-37x, and Unevictable reports 0
  throughout.  So: mlock by default (MOE_EXPERT_GTT_MLOCK=0 is the kill switch), the extent
  clamped to RLIMIT_MEMLOCK, a DECLINE with the fix when the model fits in RAM anyway, and a
  REFUSAL with the shortfall when the model cannot run without the store and it cannot be locked
  (0.76 s on a 123 GiB model instead of the 2026-10-19 over-commit).  mlock is free at creation.
- P3c (the MTP/nextn HEAD): the head's expert tables are PINNED at full residency and are NOT part of
  `-lme`'s arithmetic -- the head is metadata overhead read on every draft step, so the policy does not
  get to trade it away and its bytes sit on top of the budget (extent = `-lme N` + head).  The partition
  is by layer (`>= n_layer_trunk`) and only when the nextn layers are actually loaded (`load_mtp`), so a
  load without a drafter no longer counts -- or stores, or reads -- tensors no graph will touch.
- P3c follow-up (a SEPARATE drafter model -- Flash-Next's `mtp-...-shared-*.gguf`, one qwen4exp nextn
  block with 3 expert tables): the GTT store is ONE region per device per process, so a second load
  must not size it, grow it, take the arena tier (its extent is the trunk's budget and the cache
  reserves from the same free list) or ask for a carve it cannot get.  It now sizes its placement
  against what is actually free, adopts the live region when its set fits there, and declines cleanly
  (its layer's device buffer, which on UMA is the same host RAM and already fully resident) with a
  message that says why.  Two bugs fixed with it: a failed carve returned a null buffer and the OLD
  comment claimed the loader fell back -- it does not, the model FAILS to load (measured: `unable to
  allocate ROCmGTTStore0 buffer`, exit 1, on `-lme 1` + a separate drafter); and the store buffer's
  free path released nothing, so a second model in one process (a reload, or `llama-bench -m A -m B`)
  found the region exhausted and silently ran on device buffers -- i.e. the two rows were measured
  under different expert tiers.
- the DRAFT-side invariant (maintainer, 2026-11-11): the draft weights, embedded OR a separate file, are
  never evicted.  The embedded head is pinned at full residency (one slot per expert, so its own policy
  can never need to evict) and every path that could otherwise take it away now skips it explicitly: the
  pressure stand-down (`moe_cache_shrink_step`), the partial shrink (`moe_cache_shrink_arena`) and the
  post-drop re-arm.  The census asserts it: `MTP/nextn head residency: N table(s), S/E slots resident,
  X eviction(s)`, with an ERROR if X != 0 or S != E.  A SEPARATE drafter's tables are a whole-set device
  allocation that is not a cache table at all, so they cannot be evicted either.
- P4a (on r262): the tier's per-expert fill reads through r262's ADAPTIVE host-read transport (the
  `map -> file -> dio` ladder driven by `--load-mode auto|mmap|buffered|dio` and `MOE_HOST_POOL_TRANSPORT`,
  with the stall detector and the probe-fill A/B) instead of the legacy one-shot `g_pool_dio` choice.
  Two bugs had to be fixed for that to be real: r262 initialises the ladder at the first POOL build, and
  the GTT tier has no pool (pinning is refused on an integrated device), so a pin or `--load-mode
  buffered|dio` was silently ignored (measured: both reported `map`); and the per-table file source was
  registered only when the pool was on, so the `file`/`dio` arms could be SELECTED and then fall back to
  the mapping memcpy (measured: an escalated arm with zero storage reads).
- P4b (the destination side): on the `file` (buffered) arm a fill reads STRAIGHT into the arena slot -- no
  bounce entry, no H2D (`MOE_EXPERT_GTT_FILL_DIRECT=0` is the A/B and the kill switch).  The arena is
  registered host memory (probe 12: a pread into it is legal and coherent), the buffered arm has no
  alignment constraint, and the host write is drained behind the slot's previous consumer (counted; 0.005
  ms/fill).  `dio` keeps the bounce path (it needs the 4096 round-out plus a tail splice, because a report
  may overrun into the NEXT slot's head) and `map` keeps it too (a direct host memcpy would need that
  ordering without a sync to hide behind).  A capturing stream declines the direct path -- a synchronize
  is illegal inside a capture -- and says so in the census.
- P4f (the start arm, maintainer's Option 1): on **RDNA3_5 with the GTT arena tier and the direct fill
  available**, the transport ladder STARTS on the buffered arm instead of r262's optimistic `map`.  Three
  gates (`g_gtt_arena`, `GGML_CUDA_CC_IS_RDNA3_5`, the direct fill available) keep it off every other
  configuration -- the discrete host pool keeps r262's start exactly -- and an explicit
  `MOE_HOST_POOL_TRANSPORT` / `--load-mode` still wins.  Measured: +13.7% warm on a fitting model
  (29.0 against 25.5 t/s, and deterministic -- before this the ladder latched `file` 0 of 5 times) and
  +56-67% on a >RAM model (MBIG 7.5/7.8 against 4.5/5.0 t/s), where the set can never be cached.  The cost
  is a fitting model's FIRST run on a cold cache (-11.5%), accepted on the maintainer's steer: the cold
  condition happens once at the start, so tune for warm.
- MOE_EXPERT_GTT=0 (kill switch) reproduces today's behaviour and log byte for byte;
  MOE_EXPERT_GTT_RO=0 registers the region writable, the A/B that proves the read-rate claim.
- The ARENA tier is opt-in and stays opt-in until it has been measured on more than this box: no
  streaming/pipelined fill (P4), no prefill streaming (P5), no nextn pinning (P3c).  Without
  MOE_EXPERT_GTT_ARENA the run is the whole-tensor placement of P2, and the census says so.

Verified on halo (gfx1151, 123 GiB, ROCm 10.1.0): same-seed greedy text identical on 35B-A3B
(627b2ebd7792) and Flash-Next (f586785d7183) for store-off / auto / -lme 6 / the arena tier at
-lme 4, 6 and 8, with `--spec-type draft-mtp` and without, and a 3x residency change on the
122B-A10B gives identical text; -lme 6 realises exactly 6144.0 MiB; auto on a fitting set is the
whole set with zero evictions; registration 26 ms/GiB; pp512 within noise of the plain device
buffer for the registered READ-ONLY arm; the lock policy's four arms pass under ulimit -l 8192;
the arena tier registers all 120/144 tables, evicts under a partial budget with 0 arena releases,
and a 123.45 GiB model runs to completion at -lme 20 and -lme 60; the MTP head is pinned outside
the budget on both (3 tables / 464 MiB on 35B-A3B, 3 / 2448 MiB on the 122B) with draft acceptance
unchanged; the separate Flash-Next drafter runs in every arm (store off, `auto`, `-lme 6`, arena
`-lme 8` and the degenerate `-lme 1`) with text unchanged, the target's arena untouched, and a
two-model `llama-bench` adopts the live store for its second model instead of falling to device
buffers; the draft side never loses residency under trunk churn (`-lme 2` and `-lme 4` with 32 tokens:
`768/768 slots resident, 0 evictions` against 508 / 7670 trunk evictions; the 122B at `-lme 20`:
`768/768, 0 evictions` against 3036); the three transport arms and all four `--load-mode` values give
the same `627b2ebd7792`, warm and on a cold page cache, and an arm where every fill FAILS still does
(1886 declined + rolled back, no faults); the direct fill measures +15.6% decode warm with the heat prior frozen
(28.7/28.8/28.8 vs 24.8/24.9/25.1 t/s), the UMA start arm +13.7% (29.0 vs 25.5) and +56-67% on the >RAM
model, and every arm's text is identical in both orders; check-gpu-faults.sh clean.
